 "structural_change": "S81U-BK3 VERTICAL CUT (coordinator 0cj (b), 10-17 ~20:10): the bk clusters were ~1,160 um wide (the closed tiles' lane faces point away from the merger / control); they now stack inside the 680-um column (plan results/rtl/s81_dv_1016/bk_units_bk2/vcut_plan.json): S row 2 tiles, middle row merger-or-control + glue, N row 2 tiles (MX). Re-pinned top-down for the new neighbours; square-ish re-cut; the lane relays are gone (every hop <= ~405 um). Glue: rung on S / N (clock centred on S), W face ln0 / vd / ln2 (merger or control W of it), E face ln1 / straps / ln3. The S81U-BK2 kit s81dvbk_g (259.2 x 216, clock pin in the SW corner) measured TT insertion 457.3 / spread 128.2 ps.",
